import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
public class Solution {
	public static void sortTuples(int[][] arr) {
		int n = arr.length;
		int l = arr[0].length;

		for(int i = 1; i < n; i++){
			int key = arr[i][l-1];
			int temp[] = arr[i].clone();
			int j = i-1;


			while(j >= 0 && arr[j][l-1] > key){
				arr[j+1] = arr[j].clone();
				j--;
			}
			arr[j+1] = temp;
		}
	}
}

You are given an array of tuples ‘ARR’ of length ‘N’. All the tuples are of length ‘L’. Sort the tuples in non-decreasing order by the last element of tuples. 
If the last element of two tuples are equal then the tuple with the smallest index should be placed first.

Note: The length of all the tuples will be the same.

Example:
Input: ‘N’ = 3, ‘L’ = 2,  ‘ARR’ = [(1, 1), (5, 3), (8, 2)]. 

T.C => O(N.L)
S.C => O(L)


Output: [(1, 1), (8, 2), (5, 3)].
